===========================================================================
REQUIRED: OptiTrack's official Python NatNet SDK client
===========================================================================
This script does NOT include NatNetClient.py -- that is vendor code you
must download yourself from OptiTrack (Developer Tools -> NatNet SDK),
matching the NatNet/Motive version you actually run. Place NatNetClient.py
(and its companion files, typically DataDescriptions.py and MoCapData.py)
in the same folder as this script.
 
Exact attribute/method names for reading Rigid Body ID<->Name descriptions
have changed slightly across NatNet SDK versions over the years. The
build_rigid_body_map() method below is written against the most common
recent (NatNet 4.x) sample structure, but is clearly marked below with a
comment showing exactly what to check/adjust in YOUR downloaded
NatNetClient.py if it raises an AttributeError -- the same debugging
approach that found the real bugs in the MATLAB natnet.m wrapper earlier
in this project. If it errors, paste the exact error here and we'll fix
that one spot together, the same way.
 
===========================================================================
Dependencies (pip install):
    pip install numpy scipy matplotlib
===========================================================================
"""
 
